## Project Goal

The goal is to build and document a realistic enterprise IT environment that demonstrates identity management, endpoint administration, automation, troubleshooting, security controls, user lifecycle management, and IT service management.


### Planned Uses

- Incident management
- Service requests
- User onboarding
- User offboarding
- Assignment groups
- Ticket documentation
- IT service management workflows

## Planned Virtual Machine Resources

| VM | CPU | RAM | Storage |
|---|---|---|---|
| DC01 | 2 vCPU | 4 GB | 60 GB |
| SRV01 | 2 vCPU | 4 GB | 60 GB |
| WIN11-01 | 2 vCPU | 6 GB | 64 GB |
| WIN11-02 | 2 vCPU | 6 GB | 64 GB |

These resource allocations are initial estimates and may be adjusted based on available host hardware.

## Infrastructure Dependencies

The infrastructure will be built in the following general order:

1. Windows Server infrastructure
2. Active Directory and DNS
3. DHCP and file services
4. Windows client deployment
5. Group Policy
6. PowerShell automation
7. Microsoft Entra ID
8. Hybrid identity
9. Microsoft 365
10. Microsoft Intune
11. ServiceNow
12. Enterprise troubleshooting scenarios

## Project Goal

The infrastructure will provide a realistic enterprise environment for practicing Windows Server administration, identity management, endpoint management, cloud integration, PowerShell automation, troubleshooting, security controls, and IT service management.
